2. In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires —
“alternative classification marking”, for any classification rating, means a character or character and number prescribed by this Order as an alternative classification marking for that classification rating, regardless of font, size, proportion or colour;
“classification marking”, for any classification rating, means all the following prescribed by this Order as a classification marking for that classification rating:
(a)the character or number or both;
(b)the symbol;
(c)the symbol box, being a square, rectangle, circle or other shape;
(d)the colour of the character, number and symbol, and the background of the symbol box.
